rande near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 7.5 feet, Major Flood. Water reaches base of Twin\nMountain Bridge on Hanna Lane Road west of Del Norte. At 6.5 feet,\nwater begins flowing over Hanna Lane Road west of Del Norte. Homes\nnear First Street and the Oak Street Bridge on Colorado Highway 112\nare threatened by high water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:45 PM MST Monday the stage was 5.8 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:45 PM MST Monday was 6.6 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage just\nafter midnight tonight and continue falling to 3.4 feet Saturday\nafternoon.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-03T20:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6464bc0887f8877bfebebb5f7c89a143087a5c77.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6464bc0887f8877bfebebb5f7c89a143087a5c77.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T11:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 031120 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 420 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Windy across the plains early today. - Unsettled pattern in place through Saturday. - Drier and warmer conditions return early next week. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH TONIGHT/... Issued at 125 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 Today - Tonight: For Tuesday, relatively quiet weather ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T08:29:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 030829 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 129 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-040830- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaf